{"nodes": [{"id": "c:semi-coh-push", "type": "corollary", "title": "c:semi-coh-push", "chapter": "Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "group": "ch:Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "level": "fine", "order": 27, "statement": "Suppose $f:S \\to T$ is a morphism of eventually coconnective affine schemes\nwith $S$ semi-coherent. Then $f_*^{\\IndCoh}$ is $t$-exact.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "8cf57c28e820"}, {"id": "p:semi-coh", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:semi-coh", "chapter": "Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "group": "ch:Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "level": "medium", "order": 28, "statement": "The (classical) commutative algebra $A_n$ defined in \\S \\ref{ss:coords} is\nsemi-coherent.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "15805b56a333"}, {"id": "p:tilde-z-gens", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:tilde-z-gens", "chapter": "Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "group": "ch:Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "level": "medium", "order": 29, "statement": "For\n$n > 0$, the DG category $\\IndCoh^*(\\widetilde{\\sZ}^{\\leq n})$ is compactly\ngenerated by the objects\n$\\{\\iota_*^{r,\\IndCoh}(\\sO_{\\widetilde{\\sZ}^{\\leq n}})\\}_{r \\geq 0}$.\n\nFor $n = 0$, the DG category $\\IndCoh^*(\\widetilde{\\sZ}^{\\leq 0})$ is compactly\ngenerated by $\\sO_{\\widetilde{\\sZ}^{\\leq 0}})$.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "8baa34bd1ba6"}, {"id": "c:z-gen", "type": "corollary", "title": "c:z-gen", "chapter": "Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "group": "ch:Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "level": "fine", "order": 30, "statement": "The category $\\IndCoh^*(\\sZ^{\\leq n})$ is compactly generated\nby the objects $\\iota_*^{r,\\IndCoh}(\\sO_{\\sZ^{\\leq n}})(m)$, where $r \\geq 0$ and\n$m \\in \\bZ$.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "66084e1f1849"}, {"id": "p:y-t-str", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:y-t-str", "chapter": "Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "group": "ch:Coherent sheaves on $\\sY$", "level": "medium", "order": 31, "statement": "There is a unique $t$-structure on $\\IndCoh^*(\\sY)$ such that the\nfunctor $\\Oblv:\\IndCoh^*(\\sY) \\to \\IndCoh^*(\\sY_{\\log})$ is $t$-exact.\nMoreover, the functor $\\Av_!^{\\Gr_{\\bG_m},w}$ is $t$-exact.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "50ae50027c3d"}, {"id": "t:trun-lcft", "type": "theorem", "title": "t:trun-lcft", "chapter": "Compatibility with class field theory", "group": "ch:Compatibility with class field theory", "level": "medium", "order": 36, "statement": "The functor \\eqref{eq:trun-lcft} is an equivalence.\nIn particular, there is a canonical fully faithful symmetric monoidal functor\n$D(\\fL_n^+\\bG_m) \\into \\QCoh(\\LocSys_{\\bG_m}^{\\leq n})$.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "1575573560b2"}, {"id": "t:full-lcft", "type": "theorem", "title": "t:full-lcft", "chapter": "Compatibility with class field theory", "group": "ch:Compatibility with class field theory", "level": "medium", "order": 37, "statement": "There is a canonical symmetric monoidal equivalence:\n\n\\[\nD^*(\\fL\\bG_m) \\isom \\QCoh(\\LocSys_{\\bG_m}).\n\\]", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "052f51ec406f"}, {"id": "p:eq", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:eq", "chapter": "Compatibility with class field theory", "group": "ch:Compatibility with class field theory", "level": "medium", "order": 38, "statement": "The functor $\\ol{\\Delta}_n$ is canonically a morphism of\n$D(\\fL_n^+\\bG_m)$-module categories.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "c4c9f7ceb94d"}, {"id": "p:ff", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:ff", "chapter": "Fully faithfulness", "group": "ch:Fully faithfulness", "level": "medium", "order": 40, "statement": "For every $n \\geq 0$, the functor $\\Delta_n$ is fully faithful.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "aa2c803d1b83"}, {"id": "p:zeta", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:zeta", "chapter": "Fully faithfulness", "group": "ch:Fully faithfulness", "level": "medium", "order": 41, "statement": "For any $n > 0$, the map:\n\n\\[\n\\ul{\\End}_{\\IndCoh^*(\\LocSys_{\\bG_m}^{\\leq n})}(\n\\widetilde{\\pi}_{n,*}^{\\IndCoh}\\sO_{\\LocSys_{\\bG_m}^{\\leq n}}) \\to\n\\ul{\\End}_{\\IndCoh^*(\\sY^{\\leq n})}(\n\\zeta_*^{\\IndCoh}\\widetilde{\\pi}_{n,*}^{\\IndCoh}\n\\sO_{\\LocSys_{\\bG_m,\\log}^{\\leq n}})\n\\]\n\n is an isomorphism.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "cae5ef781108"}, {"id": "p:gr-hom", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:gr-hom", "chapter": "Fully faithfulness", "group": "ch:Fully faithfulness", "level": "medium", "order": 42, "statement": "In the above setting, suppose $M,N \\in B\\mod^{\\bG_m,w}$ with\n$M$ concentrated in non-negative graded\\footnote{As opposed to cohomological.}\ndegrees and $N$ concentrated in degree $0$.\n\nThen the natural map:\n\n\\[\n\\ul{\\Hom}_{B\\mod^{\\bG_m,w}}(M,N) \\to\n\\ul{\\Hom}_{A\\mod^{\\bG_m,w}}(\\iota_*M,\\iota_* N)\n\\]\n\n is an isomorphism.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "f03a7f404145"}, {"id": "c:gr-hom", "type": "corollary", "title": "c:gr-hom", "chapter": "Fully faithfulness", "group": "ch:Fully faithfulness", "level": "fine", "order": 43, "statement": "Suppose $\\sG \\in \\QCoh(\\LocSys_{\\bG_m,\\log}^{\\leq n})$. Then the morphism:\n\n\\[\n\\ul{\\Hom}_{\\QCoh(\\sZ^{\\leq n})}(\\sO_{\\sZ^{\\leq n}},\\widetilde{\\zeta}_* \\sG) \\to\n\\ul{\\Hom}_{\\QCoh(\\sZ^{\\leq n})}(\\iota_*\\sO_{\\sZ^{\\leq n}},\\iota_*\\widetilde{\\zeta}_* \\sG)\n\\]\n\n is an isomorphism. More generally,\nfor any $r,s \\geq 0$, the morphism:\n\n\\[\n\\ul{\\Hom}_{\\QCoh(\\sZ^{\\leq n})}(\\iota_*^r(\\sO_{\\sZ^{\\leq n}}),\\iota_*^s\\widetilde{\\zeta}_* \\sG) \\to\n\\ul{\\Hom}_{\\QCoh(\\sZ^{\\leq n})}(\\iota_*^{r+1}(\\sO_{\\sZ^{\\leq n}}),\\iota_*^{s+1}\\widetilde{\\zeta}_* \\sG)\n\\]\n\n is an isomorphism.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "d6d9fb586e4c"}, {"id": "p:loop-rep", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:loop-rep", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 8, "statement": "Suppose $Z$ is an affine scheme almost of finite type.\nThen $\\fL^+ Z$ is an affine scheme and $\\fL Z$ is an\nindscheme.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "a2886706d31d"}, {"id": "p:locsys-log", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:locsys-log", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 9, "statement": "The map:\n\n\\[\n\\LocSys_{\\bG_m,\\log} \\to \\fL^{pol} \\bA^1 dt \\times \\bB \\bG_m\n\\]\n\n is an isomorphism.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "683aca331bf1"}, {"id": "p:locsys", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:locsys", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 10, "statement": "There is an isomorphism $\\LocSys_{\\bG_m} \\simeq\n\\bA^1/\\bZ \\times \\Ker(\\Res)_{dR} \\times \\bB \\bG_m$ fitting\ninto a commutative diagram:\n\n\\[\n\\text{[Diagram omitted; see source PDF.]}\n\\]", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "aaaf35cbf899"}, {"id": "p:locsys-trun", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:locsys-trun", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 11, "statement": "The isomorphisms from Propositions \\ref{p:locsys-log} and \\ref{p:locsys}\ninduce further isomorphisms:\n\n\\[\n\\text{[Diagram omitted; see source PDF.]}\n\\]\n\n and:\n\n\\[\n\\text{[Diagram omitted; see source PDF.]}\n\\]", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "6f4b3e426cbe"}, {"id": "t:cl", "type": "theorem", "title": "t:cl", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 12, "statement": "$\\sY$ is a classical prestack.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "7866c6917e77"}, {"id": "p:zn-algebraic", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:zn-algebraic", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 13, "statement": "The prestack $\\sZ^{\\leq n}$ is a (DG) algebraic\\footnote{We refer to\n\\cite{dennis-dag} for the definition.} stack.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "5598b45dcc98"}, {"id": "c:flat-d", "type": "corollary", "title": "c:flat-d", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "fine", "order": 14, "statement": "Fix a linear map $T:\\bA^{2n} \\to \\bA^n$.\nThen $\\mu_n+T:\\bA^{2n} \\to \\bA^n$ is flat.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "e860bed1cb88"}, {"id": "c:flat-mult-infty", "type": "corollary", "title": "c:flat-mult-infty", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "fine", "order": 15, "statement": "The map:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{gathered}\n\\mu_{\\infty}:\\bA^{\\infty} \\times \\bA^{\\infty} \\to \\bA^{\\infty}\n\\\\\n\\big((a_0,a_1,\\ldots),(b_0,b_1,\\ldots)\\big) \\mapsto\n(a_0b_0,a_0b_1+a_1b_0,\\ldots,\\sum_{i = 0}^{j} a_ib_{j-i},\\ldots)\n\\end{gathered}\n\\]\n\n is flat.\n\nMore generally, suppose we are given linear maps\n$T_n:\\bA^{2n} \\to \\bA^n$ fitting into commutative diagrams:\n\n\\[\n\\text{[Diagram omitted; see source PDF.]}\n\\]\n\n with vertical maps induced by the projection\n$\\bA^{n+1} \\xar{(a_0,\\ldots,a_n) \\mapsto (a_0,\\ldots,a_{n-1})} \\bA^n$.\nLet $T$ denote the induced map\n$\\bA^{\\infty} \\times \\bA^{\\infty} \\to \\bA^{\\infty}$.\n\nThen $\\mu_{\\infty}+T$ is flat.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "a3ee4b48b7e1"}, {"id": "p:flat-axis", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:flat-axis", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 16, "statement": "The above map is flat along the axes.\nMoreover, there is a canonical isomorphism:\n\n\\[\n\\mu_{n-1}^{-1}(0) \\times \\bA^1 \\simeq Z \\underset{C}{\\times} \\bA_x^1\n\\]\n\n given by:\n\n\n\\[\n\\big((a_0,a_1,\\ldots,a_{n-2},b_0,\\ldots,b_{n-2}),\\lambda\\big) \\in\n\\mu_{n-1}^{-1}(0) \\times \\bA^1 \\mapsto\n(a_0,a_1,\\ldots,a_{n-2},\\lambda,0,b_0,b_1,\\ldots,b_{n-2}) \\in Z.\n\\]", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "2652aa86d051"}, {"id": "c:flat-axis-d", "type": "corollary", "title": "c:flat-axis-d", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "fine", "order": 17, "statement": "Suppose:\n\n\\[\nT:\\bA^{2n} = \\bA^{n} \\times \\bA^{n} \\to 0 \\times \\bA^{n-1} \\subset \\bA^n\n\\]\n\n is a linear map.\n\nLet $Z^q = (\\mu_n+T)^{-1}(0)$. Then the natural map\n$Z^q \\xar{(a_0,b_0)} C$ is flat along the axes.\n\nMoreover, in the notation of Corollary \\ref{c:flat-mult-infty}, we may take\n$n = \\infty$ in this result.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "a6b084da4613"}, {"id": "p:zn-cl", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:zn-cl", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 18, "statement": "For every $n \\geq 0$, $\\sZ^{\\leq n}$ is a\nclassical algebraic stack.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "801445074a4e"}, {"id": "p:z-flat-axes", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:z-flat-axes", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 19, "statement": "Suppose $n>0$.\n\n\\begin{enumerate}\n\n\\item \n\n\nThe map $\\sZ^{\\leq n} \\to C/\\bG_m$ is flat\nalong the axes.\\footnote{By this, we mean that the\ncorresponding map $\\sZ^{\\leq n} \\underset{\\bB\\bG_m}\\times \\Spec(k) \\to C$ is flat along the axes in the\nsense of \\S \\ref{ss:refinement}.}\n\n\\item \n\n\nWe have a canonical isomorphism:\n\n\\[\n\\sZ^{\\leq n} \\underset{C/\\bG_m}{\\times} \\bA^1/\\bG_m\n\\simeq \\sZ^{\\leq n-1}.\n\\]\n\n\\item \n\n\nLet $\\iota:\\sZ^{\\leq n} \\to \\sZ^{\\leq n}$\ndenote the map:\n\n\\[\n(\\sL,\\nabla,s) \\mapsto (\\sL(1),\\nabla,s)\n\\]\n\n\nwhere $\\sL(1)$ is the line bundle on the disc\nwhose sections on the disc are allowed\nto have a pole of order $1$ at the base-point $0 \\in \\sD$.\\footnote{Another way to say this:\n$\\Gr_{\\bG_m}$ acts on $\\sY_{\\log}$, and the corresponding\naction of $1 \\in \\bZ = \\Gr_{\\bG_m}(k)$ preserves\n$\\sZ^{\\leq n}$ for all $n$; the induced map\n$\\sZ^{\\leq n} \\to \\sZ^{\\leq n}$ is our $\\iota$.}\n\nThen $\\iota$ fits into a (derived) Cartesian diagram:\n\n\\[\n\\text{[Diagram omitted; see source PDF.]}\n\\]\n\n\\end{enumerate}", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "5b84b830adc4"}, {"id": "c:iota-afp", "type": "corollary", "title": "c:iota-afp", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "fine", "order": 20, "statement": "The above morphism\n$\\iota:\\sZ^{\\leq n} \\into \\sZ^{\\leq n}$ is an\nalmost finitely presented\\footnote{See\n\\cite{higheralgebra} Definition 7.2.4.26\nfor the definition in the affine case.\nIn the following remark in \\emph{loc. cit}., it is shown\nthat this notion is preserved under base-change.\nBy \\cite{sag} Proposition 4.1.4.3, this condition\ncan be checked flat locally. Therefore, there\nis an evident notion of a representable\nmorphism of prestacks being locally almost of finite\npresentation, and we are using the term in this\nsense.\n\nWe emphasize that in this setting,\npassing to an affine cover of $\\sZ^{\\leq n}$,\nthe corresponding map of classical affine\nschemes is a finitely presented morphism in the sense\nof classical algebraic geometry,\nbut being almost finitely presented is a\n\\emph{stronger} notion (in spite of the terminology):\nin the more classical reference \\cite{sga-6}\nExpos\\'e III D\\'efinition 1.2, this property\nof a morphism is called \\emph{pseudo-coherence}.}\nclosed embedding.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "33ab51bc0a91"}, {"id": "c:yn-log-cl", "type": "corollary", "title": "c:yn-log-cl", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "fine", "order": 21, "statement": "$\\sY_{\\log}^{\\leq n}$ is a classical ind-algebraic stack.\nMore precisely, the total space of the canonical $\\bG_m$-\ntorsor on\n$\\sY_{\\log}^{\\leq n}$ is classical and a reasonable indscheme\nin the sense of \\cite{methods} \\S 6.8.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "0085467f10c1"}, {"id": "p:z-flat-axes-var", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:z-flat-axes-var", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 22, "statement": "The map\n$\\sZ^{\\leq n} \\to \\bA^1/\\bG_m \\times \\bA^1/\\bG_m$ factors\nthrough $C/(\\bG_m\\times\\bG_m)$. For $n>0$,\nthe resulting map\n$\\sZ^{\\leq n} \\to C/(\\bG_m\\times\\bG_m)$ is flat along\naxes.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "3a18eaeacb68"}, {"id": "p:zn-coords", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:zn-coords", "chapter": "Geometry of the spectral side", "group": "ch:Geometry of the spectral side", "level": "medium", "order": 23, "statement": "The above map\n$\\Spec(A_n)/\\bG_m \\to \\sZ^{\\leq n}$ is an isomorphism.\nI.e., we have a $\\bG_m$-equivariant isomorphism\n$\\Spec(A_n) \\simeq \\widetilde{\\sZ}^{\\leq n}$.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "04b5ff2150f3"}, {"id": "t:main", "type": "theorem", "title": "Thm. \\ref{t:main-precise}", "chapter": "Introduction", "group": "ch:Introduction", "level": "medium", "order": 2, "statement": "There is a canonical equivalence of DG categories:\n\n\\[\n\\Delta:D^!(\\fL \\bA^1) \\simeq \\IndCoh^*(\\sY).\n\\]\n\nMoreover, this equivalence is compatible with the local geometric\nclass field theory of Beilinson-Drinfeld.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "b16dcd29f433"}, {"id": "p:cc-log", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:cc-log", "chapter": "Local Abel-Jacobi morphisms", "group": "ch:Local Abel-Jacobi morphisms", "level": "medium", "order": 25, "statement": "Each of the morphisms:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{gathered}\n\\Gamma^{\\IndCoh}(\\Gr_{\\bG_m}^{pos},\\omega_{\\Gr_{\\bG_m}^{pos}})\n\\to \\Gamma(\\fL^+ \\bA^1,\\sO_{\\fL^+ \\bA^1}) \\\\\n\\Gamma^{\\IndCoh}(\\Gr_{\\bG_m},\\omega_{\\Gr_{\\bG_m}})\n\\to \\Gamma(\\fL^+ \\bG_m,\\sO_{\\fL^+ \\bG_m}) \\\\\n\\Gamma^{\\IndCoh}(\\Gr_{\\bG_m}^{pos,\\leq n},\\omega_{\\Gr_{\\bG_m}^{pos,\\leq n}})\n\\to \\Gamma(\\fL_n^+ \\bA^1,\\sO_{\\fL_n^+ \\bA^1}) \\\\\n\\Gamma^{\\IndCoh}(\\Gr_{\\bG_m}^{\\leq n},\\omega_{\\Gr_{\\bG_m}^{\\leq n}})\n\\to \\Gamma(\\fL_n^+ \\bG_m,\\sO_{\\fL_n^+ \\bA^1})\n\\end{gathered}\n\\]\n\n coming from our pairings and \\S \\ref{ss:pairing-map}\nis an isomorphism.\n\nMoreover, each isomorphism is a map of commutative algebras,\nwhere the left hand sides are commutative algebras using\nthe commutative monoid structures on the relevant spaces,\nwhile the right hand sides are commutative algebras\nas functions on schemes.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "34c9d79b2145"}, {"id": "p:delta-infty-comm", "type": "proposition", "title": "p:delta-infty-comm", "chapter": "Proof of the main theorem", "group": "ch:Proof of the main theorem", "level": "medium", "order": 45, "statement": "There exist unique commutative diagrams \\eqref{eq:delta-infty-comm}\nso that the resulting map \\eqref{eq:delta-can-n} is \\eqref{eq:delta-delta}.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "548e973d2ba8"}, {"id": "t:main-precise", "type": "theorem", "title": "t:main-precise", "chapter": "Proof of the main theorem", "group": "ch:Proof of the main theorem", "level": "medium", "order": 46, "statement": "There is a unique equivalence:\n\n\\[\n\\Delta:D^!(\\fL\\bA^1) \\isom  \\IndCoh^*(\\sY)\n\\]\n\n of $D^*(\\fL\\bG_m)$-module categories such that the induced morphism:\n\n\\[\nD^!(\\fL^+\\bA^1) \\subset D^!(\\fL\\bA^1) \\to \\IndCoh^*(\\sY)\n\\]\n\n of $D^*(\\fL^{pos}\\bG_m)$-module categories coincides with the functor\n$\\Delta_{\\infty}$ from above.", "uses": [], "sources": ["tates-thesis-de-rham-setting"], "lean_name": null, "proved": false, "mathlib_ok": false, "lean_status": "empty", "state": "ready", "unlocks": 0, "lean_source": null, "has_sorry": false, "lean_file": null, "dep_count": 0, "rdep_count": 0, "descendant_count": 0, "comment_count": 0, "review_count": 0, "hgraph_id": "1c38ecd74e18"}], "edges": [], "dangling": [], "meta": {"engine": "hgraph", "entry": "/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/FormalizedPapers/ArithmeticGeometry/TatesThesisDeRhamSetting/blueprint/src/content.tex", "macros": {"\\label": "", "\\source": "", "\\dcref": "", "\\uses": "", "\\lean": "", "\\leanok": "", "\\mathlibok": "", "\\notready": "", "\\Spec": "\\on{Spec}", "\\Pic": "\\on{Pic}", "\\Jac": "\\operatorname{Jac}", "\\GL": "\\operatorname{GL}", "\\Hom": "\\on{Hom}", "\\End": "\\on{End}", "\\C": "\\mathbb{C}", "\\Q": "\\mathbb{Q}", "\\Z": "\\mathbb{Z}", "\\F": "\\mathbb{F}", "\\P": "\\mathbb{P}", "\\A": "\\mathbb{A}"